# Atlas CODEOWNERS — this file is the risk-class boundary.
#
# It decides which changes need the OWNER's tap and which the independent
# reviewer can clear on its own. There is deliberately NO catch-all: ordinary
# product code requires no code-owner review, so a reviewer GO plus green tests
# lets GitHub auto-merge it with zero taps. The paths below are the GUARDED
# surfaces — schema, auth, money, infrastructure, and Atlas's own controls —
# where a mistake is expensive or irreversible. Touching any of them requires
# @steve-rangerandfox review no matter what the reviewer says. The machine
# account (rangerfox-atlas) is deliberately kept OUT of this file: a non-owner's
# approval must never satisfy the gate.
#
# atlas-os note: this is the governance repo itself, so it guards MORE than the
# generic template. Beyond the hooks, it guards the human-authority CLI
# (scripts/), the templates propagated to every adopted repo, and the schemas
# that define durable state — because an unreviewed change to any of those
# silently weakens the boundary in every downstream project at once. Ordinary
# prose (skills/*.md, agents/*.md, docs, spec, adr, README) is NOT guarded: the
# independent reviewer's GO clears it, and it auto-merges with no owner tap.

# --- Atlas's own enforcement, authority, and propagated surface ---
/.atlas/**                         @steve-rangerandfox
/plugin/atlas/hooks/**             @steve-rangerandfox
/plugin/atlas/scripts/**           @steve-rangerandfox
/plugin/atlas/templates/**         @steve-rangerandfox
/plugin/atlas/schemas/**           @steve-rangerandfox
/.claude/**                        @steve-rangerandfox
/CLAUDE.md                         @steve-rangerandfox
/AGENTS.md                         @steve-rangerandfox

